http://dag.github.io/cll/7/6/

For good examples of =93nei=94 and =93no'a=94, we need nested bridi context=
s:

6.14)  mi se pluka le nu do pensi
             le nu nei kei pu le nu do zukte
       I am-pleased-by the event-of (you think-about
             (the event-of [main bridi]) before the-event of (your acting).
       I am pleased that you thought about whether I
             would be pleased (about ...) before you acted.
6.15)  mi ba klama ca le nu do no'a
       I [future] go [present] the event-of you [repeats outer bridi]
       I will go when you do.


Acc. to jvs {nei} =3D pro-bridi: repeats the current bridi.

So the CLL contradicts it.

I also don't understand the meaning of example 6.14) if we assume {nei}=20
refers to the current bridi, not the main bridi (the one that has {se=20
pluka} as a selbri).

I suggest removing 6.14) and replacing it with something having the correct=
=20
usage of {nei}.
I suggested {mi lumci lo nei} (I wash myself) but JCowan said there could=
=20
be much better examples.

